---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FAQ | Springfield Lot Striping"
  description="Frequently asked questions about commercial parking lot striping in Springfield, MO, including restriping timing, ADA marking, fire lanes, documentation, and service areas."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-concrete">
      <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p>These answers are written for commercial buyers in Springfield and Greene County who need parking lot striping, restriping, ADA marking, fire lanes, and warehouse line work.</p>

      <h2>How often should a commercial lot be restriped?</h2>
      <p>Most commercial lots need restriping every 12 to 24 months depending on traffic volume, weather exposure, sealcoating schedules, and how quickly the existing paint fades. High-traffic properties may need attention sooner.</p>

      <h2>Do you handle ADA compliance striping?</h2>
      <p>Yes. ADA-related striping often includes accessible stalls, van-accessible spaces, access aisles, and related layout updates. Buyers should still verify final compliance requirements with their inspector or accessibility professional before work begins.</p>

      <h2>Can striping be done while the property stays open?</h2>
      <p>Usually, yes. Many commercial projects are phased, scheduled overnight, or completed during low-traffic windows so tenants and customers can still access the property.</p>

      <h2>What information should I include in a quote request?</h2>
      <p>Include the city, property type, approximate stall count, current lot condition, whether the work is new layout or restriping, and any compliance or deadline concerns. Photos are helpful too.</p>

      <h2>Do you serve outside Springfield?</h2>
      <p>Yes. The site supports commercial striping requests across Springfield, Nixa, Ozark, Republic, Battlefield, and Rogersville, plus nearby Greene County and surrounding service areas as needed.</p>

      <h2>Do you provide documentation?</h2>
      <p>Commercial buyers usually want before-and-after photos, stall counts, or other job documentation. Include that request in the form so the provider knows what records you need.</p>

      <h2>How do I get started?</h2>
      <p>Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> or the homepage quote form. The request is most useful when it includes the property location, timing, and the exact marking work needed.</p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
